  "analysis": "We need to compute the maximum number of 11-digit phone numbers of the form '8' followed by 10 digits, using each card at most once. Let c8 be the count of '8' digits in the input, and rest be the number of non-'8' digits (n - c8). To form k numbers, we need k '8's and 10k other digits, so k <= c8 and 10k <= rest. The maximum k is min(c8, floor(rest/10)). If this value is 0, no number can be formed. The problem constraints (n <= 100) are small, so a simple O(n) solution is sufficient. We will implement a small Python script to read input, compute c8 and rest, and print the result.",
